IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Consumer Guarantees Act 1993 (New Zealand) — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Every fact the rule modules read, and nothing else: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1993_91.txt (New Zealand
-- Legislation, version as at 24 January 2026, converted from the PCO XML).
-- Field names are unique across records.

§ `Consumer Guarantees Act 1993 — the nouns`

§§ `The acquirer and the supply (ss 2, 41, 43, 56)`

-- s 2 "consumer means a person who— (a) acquires from a supplier goods or
-- services of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic, or
-- household use or consumption; and (b) does not acquire the goods or
-- services, or hold himself or herself out as acquiring [them], for the
-- purpose of— (i) resupplying them in trade; or (ii) consuming them in the
-- course of a process of production or manufacture; or (iii) in the case of
-- goods, repairing or treating in trade other goods or fixtures on land".
DECLARE Acquirer HAS
    `of a kind ordinarily acquired for personal, domestic, or household use or consumption` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired, or held out as acquired, to resupply in trade` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired, or held out as acquired, to consume in production or manufacture` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquired, or held out as acquired, to repair or treat other goods or fixtures in trade` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 2 "goods ... (c) despite paragraph (b)(i), does not include a whole
-- building, or part of a whole building, attached to land unless the
-- building is a structure that is easily removable and is not designed for
-- residential accommodation"; s 7B gas (other than non-reticulated gas)
-- and electricity are not goods, except for s 7A.
DECLARE `Thing supplied` IS ONE OF
    `goods`
    `a building attached to land, easily removable and not designed for residential accommodation`
    `a building attached to land, of any other kind`
    `gas or electricity supplied by a gas or electricity retailer`
    `services`

-- s 43(2): a clause contracting out of the Act.
DECLARE `Contracting out clause` HAS
    `the agreement is in writing`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `supplied and acquired in trade`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `all parties are in trade`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `all parties agree to contract out`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is fair and reasonable that the parties are bound` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Supply HAS
    `thing supplied`                                    IS A `Thing supplied`
    -- s 41(1) "supplied otherwise than in trade".
    `supplied in trade`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 41(2) "supplied by the charitable organisation for the principal
    -- purpose of benefiting the person to whom the supply is made".
    `supplied by a charity for the principal purpose of benefiting the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 56 "any contract for the supply of goods or services made before the
    -- commencement of this Act".
    `contract made on`                                  IS A DATE
    `clause contracting out`                            IS A MAYBE `Contracting out clause`

§§ `Goods (Parts 1-3)`

DECLARE `Goods guarantee` IS ONE OF
    `s 5 title`
    `s 5A delivery`
    `s 6 acceptable quality`
    `s 7A acceptable quality of gas or electricity`
    `s 8 fitness for a particular purpose`
    `s 9 correspondence with description`
    `s 10 correspondence with sample`
    `s 11 price`
    `s 12 repairs and spare parts`
    `s 13 a manufacturer's express guarantee`

DECLARE `Goods failure` HAS
    `guarantee failed`                                  IS A `Goods guarantee`
    -- s 18(2)-(3) "Where the failure can be remedied"; "cannot be remedied".
    `the failure can be remedied`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 18(2)(b) "a supplier who has been required to remedy a failure
    -- refuses or neglects to do so, or does not succeed in doing so within
    -- a reasonable time".
    `the supplier refused, neglected or failed to remedy it` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 21(a)-(d).
    `a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the failure would not have acquired the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods depart in a significant respect from the description, sample or model` IS A BOOLEAN
    `substantially unfit for a common or made-known purpose, and not easily and quickly remedied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `not of acceptable quality because unsafe`          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 20(1).
    `rejected within a reasonable time`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `disposed of, or lost or destroyed away from the supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `damaged after delivery for reasons unrelated to their state at supply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `attached to property and cannot be detached without damage` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 17: the failure is only because of a representation by the
    -- manufacturer (not on packaging or a label).
    `fails acceptable quality only because of a manufacturer's representation` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(b): the description was applied by or with the consent of the
    -- manufacturer.
    `the description was applied by or with the consent of the manufacturer` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 26: the failure is only because of another person's act, default,
    -- omission or representation, or a cause independent of human control
    -- after the goods left the manufacturer, or (for acceptable quality) a
    -- price above the recommended or average retail price.
    `fails only because of another person or a cause after the goods left the manufacturer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fails acceptable quality only because the price was above the recommended or average retail price` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 25(d) "during the currency of the guarantee"; s 14 binding.
    `the express guarantee binds the manufacturer and was current` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 42: the consumer was told repairs and parts would not be available
    -- (at all, or after a period that has expired).
    `notice under s 42 excludes s 12`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 27(2): an express guarantee lets the consumer require repair or
    -- replacement, and the manufacturer was required and refused, neglected
    -- or failed.
    `an express guarantee entitles the consumer to repair or replacement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the manufacturer refused, neglected or failed to remedy it` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 5A(2)(a) and s 18(4): "of a substantial character" for delivery; the
    -- consequential loss was "reasonably foreseeable".
    `there is reasonably foreseeable consequential loss` IS A BOOLEAN
    `price paid or payable`                             IS A NUMBER
    `average retail price at the time of supply`        IS A NUMBER
    `value of the goods with the failure`               IS A NUMBER

§§ `Services (Part 4)`

DECLARE `Service guarantee` IS ONE OF
    `s 28 reasonable care and skill`
    `s 29 fitness for a particular purpose`
    `s 30 time of completion`
    `s 31 price`

DECLARE `Service failure` HAS
    `service guarantee failed`                          IS A `Service guarantee`
    `the service failure can be remedied`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier refused, neglected or failed to remedy the service` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 36(a)-(d).
    `a reasonable consumer fully acquainted with the failure would not have acquired the services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the product is substantially unfit for a common purpose and not easily and quickly remedied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the product is unfit for a made-known purpose or result and not easily and quickly remedied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the product of the service is unsafe`              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 33.
    `fails only because of another person or a cause independent of human control` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 35.
    `the service is merely incidental to goods the consumer may reject` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a contract with the supplier`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is reasonably foreseeable consequential loss from the service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `charge paid or payable`                            IS A NUMBER
    `value of the product of the service with the failure` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Remedies`

DECLARE Remedy IS ONE OF
    `require the supplier to remedy the failure within a reasonable time`
    `have the failure remedied elsewhere and recover the reasonable costs from the supplier`
    `reject the goods and choose a refund or a replacement`
    `damages from the supplier for the reduction in value`
    `damages from the supplier for reasonably foreseeable consequential loss`
    `refuse to pay more than a reasonable price`
    `cancel the contract for the service`
    `damages from the manufacturer for the reduction in value`
    `damages from the manufacturer for reasonably foreseeable consequential loss`

§§ `The case`

DECLARE `Failure complained of` IS ONE OF
    `a failure of goods` HAS
        `the goods failure`                             IS A `Goods failure`
    `a failure of a service` HAS
        `the service failure`                           IS A `Service failure`

DECLARE `Consumer case` HAS
    `the acquirer`                                      IS AN Acquirer
    `the supply`                                        IS A Supply
    `the failure`                                       IS A `Failure complained of`
